<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ananda Mahidol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Rama VIII</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ananda Mahidol, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> VIII, was king of Siam, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, from 1935 to 1946. He came to the throne aged nine after the abdication of his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prajadhipok">Prajadhipok</a> and spent most of his reign at school in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> while regents governed. Six months after returning in December 1945 he was found shot dead in his bedroom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-palace">Grand Palace</a>; his death has never been fully explained.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ananda-mahidol.jpg" alt="Ananda Mahidol" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: กรมแผนที่ทหารบก (Royal Thai Army Survey Department) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ananda_Mahidol_portrait_photograph.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
